{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794246206,"nonce":"l8LSQqWsEK7u0eMIsEdcRRBaUdE=","title":"jno.rcwa reports the incident medium's wavelength when light enters from a substrate","message":"The vector front door takes k0 from the incident-side ambient and assumes it is vacuum ('k0 from the superstrate (vacuum =\u003e coeff = k0^2)'). With the source on a dielectric substrate (index n), it infers k0' = n k0 and divides every permittivity by n^2. The solve is unchanged, since the equation only contains k0^2 eps, and T/R are right. But rc.spec.wavelength reports lambda/n, and layer permittivities read below 1 in the exit medium.\n\nReproduction: a periodic cell with the incident load on the bottom face of a substrate of index 1.56; rc.spec.wavelength = 0.641 for lambda = 1.\n\nFix direction: take k0 from the vacuum side when one ambient is vacuum, or let the absorbing-face coefficient (k_n = n k0) give n per ambient; at least name the medium in spec.","files":null}]}